First Nmap Scan: Ubuntu Web Server

Objective

Identify open TCP ports on my Ubuntu virtual machine using Nmap from Kali Linux.

Lab Setup

* Testing machine: Kali Linux
* Target machine: Ubuntu Linux
* Target IP: 192.168.56.2
* Tool: Nmap 7.94SVN
* Network: Isolated VirtualBox host-only lab network

Command Used

nmap 192.168.56.2

Results

Port	State	Service
80/tcp	Open	HTTP

Nmap reported that the host was up and that 999 of the 1,000 commonly scanned TCP ports were closed.

Analysis

The open TCP port 80 is consistent with the Apache2 web server running on Ubuntu. This confirms that the web server is reachable from Kali Linux over the lab network.

The remaining scanned ports were reported as closed. This result applies to the ports and scan conditions used in this exercise; it does not establish that every possible service or port on the system is secure.

What I Learned

* How to perform a basic Nmap TCP port scan.
* How to identify open and closed ports.
* How to connect a discovered network service to the application running on the target machine.
* Why network scanning results are useful for security assessment.

Next Steps

